+ version: 1.0.1
+ ## How to Use
+ This skill connects to a remote MCP server. No local code execution, no API keys, no credentials required from the user.
+ ### MCP Connection
+ Add to your MCP client config:
+ ```json
+ ```json
+ {
+ {
+   "mcpServers": {
+     "kr-crypto-intelligence": {
+       "url": "https://mcp.printmoneylab.com/mcp"
+     }
+   }
+ }
+ }
+ ```
+ ```
+ ### Available Tools (6)
+ | Tool | Method | Description |
+ |------|--------|-------------|
+ | `get_kimchi_premium` | MCP tool call with `symbol` param (default: "BTC") | Returns Upbit vs Binance price gap percentage |
+ | `get_stablecoin_premium` | MCP tool call, no params | Returns USDT/USDC premium on Korean exchanges |
+ | `get_kr_prices` | MCP tool call with `symbol` and `exchange` params | Returns KRW prices from Upbit/Bithumb |
+ | `get_fx_rate` | MCP tool call, no params | Returns current USD/KRW exchange rate |
+ | `get_available_symbols` | MCP tool call, no params | Returns list of tradeable symbols |
+ | `check_health` | MCP tool call, no params | Returns service and exchange connectivity status |
+ ### REST API (Alternative)
+ Tools can also be called as standard HTTP GET requests:
+ GET https://api.printmoneylab.com/api/v1/kimchi-premium?symbol=BTC
+ GET https://api.printmoneylab.com/api/v1/stablecoin-premium
+ GET https://api.printmoneylab.com/api/v1/kr-prices?symbol=ETH&exchange=all
+ GET https://api.printmoneylab.com/api/v1/fx-rate
+ GET https://api.printmoneylab.com/api/v1/symbols  (free)
+ GET https://api.printmoneylab.com/health  (free)
+ ### Example Response
+   "symbol": "BTC",
