+ ## Payment (x402 Protocol)
+ Paid endpoints return HTTP 402 with payment instructions in the `payment-required` header. The x402 protocol handles payment automatically — no wallet setup or private key needed from the skill user.
+ **How it works:**
+ 1. Agent calls a paid endpoint
+ 2. Server returns 402 with payment requirements in header
+ 3. x402-compatible client automatically signs a $0.001 USDC transfer
+ 4. Client retries with payment proof in `X-PAYMENT` header
+ 5. Server verifies and returns data
+ **Cost:** $0.001 USDC per call (~0.1 cent)
+ **Networks:** Base (eip155:8453) or Solana mainnet
+ **No credentials needed:** Payment is handled at the transport layer by x402-compatible MCP clients (e.g., xpay Smart Proxy). Users without x402 support can use the free endpoints (`/symbols`, `/health`) with no payment.
+ - **Kimchi Premium > 3%**: Strong Korean demand, potential cross-exchange arbitrage
+ - **Stablecoin Premium positive**: Capital flowing INTO Korean crypto market (bullish signal)
+ - **Stablecoin Premium negative**: Capital flowing OUT (risk-off signal)
+ - **FX rate spike**: Won weakening, may amplify crypto premium
+ ## Security
+ - **No local code execution** — instruction-only skill
+ - **No credentials stored** — no API keys, no wallet keys, no env vars
+ - **No file system access** — all data comes from remote API
+ - **Network calls only to:** `mcp.printmoneylab.com` and `api.printmoneylab.com`
